# Purpose

This project was scaffolded with the **`forge-lifecycle`** bootstrap profile. Durable cross-project lessons live in the bootstrap repository, not only here.

# Bootstrap source of lessons

Canonical integration lessons: [nicksinx/bootstrap](https://github.com/nicksinx/bootstrap) → `.okf/improvements/forge-lifecycle-bootstrap-lessons.md`

Record **project-specific** Forge outcomes under this directory (promotion failures, version pins, smoke evidence paths).

# First actions

1. Confirm HTTP `forge-collection` in Desktop MCP and, for Cloud Agents, the custom URL on cursor.com/agents (Cloud does not inherit `~/.cursor/mcp.json`).
2. `scripts/forge-clone-siblings.sh` on the Node host that will run Forge (or clone manually)
3. Build siblings. Use `.cursor/mcp-forge-stdio-siblings.json.example` only when this Cursor session should spawn local stdio servers.
4. Read `docs/forge-lifecycle-integration.md` and `.okf/decisions/0002-okf-forge-integration.md`
5. Run sibling smokes before cross-MCP handoffs. Catalog-only work needs Vercel `/api/mcp` only.

